{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When they draw near</b> — Some say: בקרוב is from the root לקרב (to draw near). Others said: [it means] when they draw near to me. Rabbi Moses said: the sense of 'my adversaries and my enemies' is specific men who were his foes."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:40.456169002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}